{"chunk_id": "aa919674bdca", "text": "Sita passionately argues that she must accompany Rama into exile. Reminding him of a prophecy that she would live in the forest and declaring absolute marital devotion, she insists that hardship beside him will feel like comfort, while life without him would be unbearable. When Rama still hesitates, she sharply rebukes him, suggesting that if he were truly brave he would not try to leave her behind. She vows that even forest thorns, dust, and austere food will seem like luxuries in his presence and threatens death if forced to remain. Overcome by her grief and resolve, Rama finally relents, explaining that he had tested her resolve and that obedience to parents is sacred, before agreeing to take her with him.\nSita passionately insists on accompanying Rama into exile, and moved by her unwavering resolve and devotion, Rama finally agrees and explains his duty to obey his father.\nThemes: marital devotion, dharma and filial duty, exile decision, steadfast resolve", "vector": [0.024908479303121567, -0.02120218425989151, -0.02342323586344719, 0.004159361589699984, -0.017931925132870674, 0.02372300997376442, -0.02763369493186474, -0.0020864938851445913, -0.02409091405570507, -0.015683621168136597, 0.013483008369803429, 0.003437179373577237, 0.014539030380547047, 0.011023500934243202, -0.015342969447374344, -0.004854292143136263, 0.05995476245880127, -0.00030318033532239497, 0.036054614931344986, -0.014375517144799232, -0.004574957303702831, -0.015056821517646313, -0.007371710613369942, -0.0029364207293838263, -0.022455783560872078, -0.007501158397644758, 0.022755557671189308, -0.02869652956724167, 0.016215037554502487, -0.020698020234704018, -0.002382861217483878, -0.013585204258561134, -0.001899135299026966, -0.028751034289598465, -0.022946322336792946, -0.003832335816696286, -0.012086335569620132, -0.0213384460657835, 0.010103740729391575, -0.01372146513313055, 0.009020466357469559, -0.0006672522285953164, -0.0194716714322567, -0.0